      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Cloudblast VPS Review 2026: €3.6/mo 10 Gbps + DDoS-Included</h1>
      <p class="text-gray-400 text-base">Last updated: August 19, 2026 · 12 min read</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none text-gray-300 leading-relaxed space-y-5">

      <p>Cloudblast surfaced on the budget-VPS radar in August 2026 with an opening offer that is unusually aggressive for the price bracket: <strong>€3.6/month for 1 vCPU / 3 GB RAM / 20 GB NVMe SSD</strong>, a <strong>10 Gbps</strong> network port, and <strong>DDoS protection bundled as standard</strong> on every plan. Most competing entry-tier VPSes at this price ship 1 Gbps ports and treat DDoS as a paid add-on. We dug into the live pricing, datacenter footprint, and hardware behind the offer — including a body-verified LowEndBox feature article and the cloudblast.io pricing page itself — to see how it stacks up against our existing <a href="/vps" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">VPSTier-covered lineup</a>.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-10 mb-4">Cloudblast at a Glance</h2>
      <p>Cloudblast is a new entrant running hourly-billed KVM/Proxmox cloud VPS on AMD EPYC host nodes, with three active locations (Amsterdam, Salt Lake City, Hong Kong) and a fourth UK site listed as "coming soon." The brand is not yet well-known outside LowEndTalk / LowEndBox, but the August 2026 <a href="https://lowendbox.com/blog/cloudblast-4gb-vps-for-only-e4-03-month-in-usa-nl-and-hong-kong-with-unlimited-bandwidth/" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">LowEndBox feature article</a> confirms it has real infrastructure, real test IPs, and a working panel.</p>

      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-300">
        <li><strong>Launched:</strong> 2026 (first major editorial coverage: LowEndBox 2026-08-12 by raindog308)</li>
        <li><strong>Niche:</strong> Hourly-billed KVM cloud VPS with DDoS-included + 10 Gbps standard</li>
        <li><strong>Hardware:</strong> AMD EPYC 7551P / 7C13 / 7663 host nodes, NVMe SSD, KVM/Proxmox virtualization</li>
        <li><strong>Network:</strong> 10 Gbps uplink + DDoS protection on every instance</li>
        <li><strong>Datacenters:</strong> 3 active (Amsterdam / Salt Lake City / Hong Kong) + 1 coming (Birmingham UK)</li>
        <li><strong>Billing:</strong> Hourly (€0.0049 – €0.109/hr) and monthly prepaid, both available</li>
        <li><strong>Payment:</strong> Credit cards (Stripe: Visa/MC/Amex), AliPay, crypto including Monero (XMR)</li>
        <li><strong>Entry plan:</strong> VMA11 at €3.6/mo (1 vCPU, 3 GB RAM, 20 GB NVMe)</li>
      </ul>

